body:
The HTML API is preferable for producing STYLE tags because it will correctly escape the tag contents and attribute values. Typical HTML escaping approaches are not available because STYLE tags contain _raw text_.

Using the HTML API is safer, and the additional safety allows for richer CSS to be embedded in STYLE tags. For example, the CSS in [ticket 64418](https://core.trac.wordpress.org/ticket/64418) which cannot be expressed without some characters like `<>`:

```css
@property --animate {
  syntax: "<custom-ident>";
  inherits: true;
  initial-value: false;
}
```

This does not fix the ticket, but is an important part of the solution to ensure that arbitrary CSS can be safely embedded inside of HTML STYLE tags.

Trac ticket: https://core.trac.wordpress.org/ticket/64418

